# Codex permission rules. Tracked deliberately: an untracked allow-list is per-machine, so
# two operators get different agent behaviour from the same task.
# Mirrors TIER 1 of the STANDING AUTHORIZATION block on every chart-backlog bead. Tiers 2 and 3
# are per-bead grants and human gates, deliberately NOT here; baking them into a machine-wide
# prefix rule erases the distinction.
#
# THE BAR IS "BOUNDED AND RECOVERABLE", NOT "READ-ONLY AND HERMETIC". Every header here asserted
# the latter until 2026-08-31 and it was false of nearly every file: most of these rules reach
# the network, and several WRITE. Each file states its own writes below. Nothing here pushes a
# git ref, mutates a cloud provider or a cluster, or merges a PR -- but bd DOES write shared
# state, so read bd.rules before assuming a grant is local.
#
# A rule constrains a command's PREFIX and nothing else -- never a flag, path or refspec that
# appears later in argv. If you cannot express the safe subset as a prefix, do not write the
# allow. Every defect found in review was a comment asserting an invariant prefix matching
# cannot enforce.
# Added 2026-08-31.
# WRITES: fmt rewrites tracked .tf files; init writes .terraform/ and may update
# .terraform.lock.hcl. Network: init and providers reach registry.opentofu.org.
# No tofu apply -- it falls through to a prompt. Not read-only: see above.
#
# REMOVED 2026-09-01, four of them, every claim MEASURED against a throwaway local root with a
# sensitive variable rather than assumed:
#   init          `tofu init -migrate-state` / `-force-copy` COPY STATE BETWEEN BACKENDS, which
#                 writes the remote backend -- flatly contradicting this header's claim that
#                 nothing here mutates a cloud provider. The flag sits later in argv.
#   state show    LEAKS. Expected to redact as "(sensitive value)"; it does not.
#   state pull    LEAKS -- raw state, no redaction at all.
#   output        plain `output` redacts, but `output -json` LEAKS. Unfixable by prefix, the
#                 same shape as `kubectl config view --raw`, so the allow goes.
# Measured clean and therefore KEPT: plan, plan -json, state list, validate (0 leaks each).
# RESIDUAL, stated: `providers lock` / `providers mirror` write locally, and `fmt` rewrites
# tracked files. Both bounded and recoverable. Running init through an enumerated `just` recipe
# is unaffected.
#
# REMOVED 2026-09-01 (round 3): "plan", and my own earlier "measured clean" claim for it was
# INCOMPLETE -- it measured stdout only. Two later flags defeat it, both MEASURED:
#   plan -show-sensitive   prints values a plain plan redacts (plan=0 hits, -show-sensitive=1)
#   plan -out=<file>       writes a plan file holding UNREDACTED sensitive values. A raw grep of
#                          that file finds nothing because it is compressed; `tofu show -json`
#                          on it returns the secret. A naive grep would have wrongly cleared it.
# Still measured clean and KEPT: validate, fmt, providers, version, state list.
prefix_rule(pattern=["tofu", ["validate", "fmt", "providers", "version"]], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["tofu", "state", "list"], decision="allow")
